## 7. Requirements

- REQ-FIG0907-01 [MUST-STANDARD] The sheet draws three distance bands, labelled `dist 0`, `dist 1`, `dist 2` at 15 units, and every vertex sits inside the band whose number equals its chip value. (source: BRIEFING section 2 distances; WCAG 1.4.1)
- REQ-FIG0907-02 [MUST-STANDARD] Vertex ids are 18 units, chip values and step notes 15, panel labels 16 semibold, the layer note 14, and no text is below 14. (source: BRIEFING section 4)
- REQ-FIG0907-03 [MUST-LOCAL] Each of the five vertices carries one chip holding a single distance digit, and no chip is blank or carries a range. (why: the chip is the per-vertex readout of band membership)
- REQ-FIG0907-04 [MUST-STANDARD] The strip shows six rows in trace order, `s`, `a b`, `b c t`, `c t`, `t`, empty, and no seventh row. (source: chapter section 9.3.2 Listing 9.1 replayed on the adjacency lists of BRIEFING section 2)
- REQ-FIG0907-05 [MUST-LOCAL] At step k the dequeued vertex carries the accent ring and its chip carries the success role at that same step, so ring and settled chip coexist on the dequeue frame. (why: finality happens at dequeue)
- REQ-FIG0907-06 [MUST-LOCAL] The note `queue holds at most` and `two consecutive layers` sits in the strip header at 14 units, two lines, with no leader. (why: the brief requires the bound stated inside the figure)
- REQ-FIG0907-07 [MUST-STANDARD] Settled chips carry a success outline at 3.2 and a filled dot; pending chips carry a muted outline at 1.6 and no dot, so no role is carried by hue alone. (source: WCAG 1.4.1)
- REQ-FIG0907-08 [MUST-STANDARD] Text reaches 4.5:1 and meaningful strokes 3:1 against their surface in both themes at the values quoted in section 5. (source: WCAG 1.4.3 and 1.4.11, BRIEFING section 5)
- REQ-FIG0907-09 [MUST-LOCAL] The five nodes sit at the canonical coordinates with the single translation y + 70 and radius 22, and no other offset. (source: BRIEFING section 3)
- REQ-FIG0907-10 [MUST-LOCAL] View A holds at least 30 live marks and view B at least 26, counted with `querySelectorAll("*").length` on each panel group. (why: roster floors, BRIEFING section 4)
